        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Duke University, Tufts University\n- People: James David Barber\n- Places: Durham, North Carolina, Trinity\n- Concepts: university founding, relocation, teaching roles\n\nFacts:\n- Duke University was founded by Methodists and Quakers in the present-day town of Trinity in 1838.\n- Tufts College was founded in 1852 by Christian Universalists who sought to create a nonsectarian institution of higher learning.\n- Duke University moved to Durham in 1892.\n- From 1977 to 1995, James David Barber taught political science at Duke University.\n- Duke University is a private research university located in Durham, North Carolina.",
